      "writingTasks": [
        {
          "summary": "In the lyric poem 'Dreams', Langston Hughes delivers a passionate plea to cherish and guard one's aspirations. Through two succinct four-line stanzas, he warns against abandoning dreams. In the first stanza, he compares a life devoid of dreams to a broken-winged bird that cannot fly, emphasizing that without dreams, the human spirit is crippled, grounded, and stripped of its natural potential to soar. In the second stanza, he portrays a dreamless existence as a barren field frozen with snow, illustrating coldness, spiritual sterility, and absolute desolation. The poem powerfully concludes that dreams are the life-giving force of human ambition and happiness.",
          "essay": {
            "title": "A Dream Doesn't Become Reality Through Magic: It Takes Sweat, Determination and Hard Work",
            "text": "Every transformative breakthrough in human civilization originated as a dream in an inspired mind. However, visionary ideas remain inert fantasies unless they are converted into tangible reality through unyielding labor, sweat, and perseverance. As Colin Powell famously observed, success requires relentless commitment rather than wishing upon stars. History is replete with icons who turned dreams into monuments of human achievement through grueling struggle. Thomas Edison endured thousands of failed experiments before illuminating the world with the electric bulb. Quaid-e-Azam Muhammad Ali Jinnah transformed the dream of an independent Pakistan into a political reality against colossal odds through intellectual discipline and unshakeable fortitude. Obstacles, setbacks, and discouragements are inevitable in any worthwhile endeavor. Those who hold fast to their dreams while willingly investing sweat, discipline, and sustained sacrifice ultimately conquer adversity and transform aspirations into enduring triumph."
          },
          "translationUrdu": [
            {
              "english": "Hold fast to dreams, for if dreams die, life is a broken-winged bird that cannot fly.",
              "urdu": "خوابوں کو مضبوطی سے تھامے رکھو، کیونکہ اگر خواب مر جائیں تو زندگی ٹوٹے ہوئے پروں والا وہ پرندہ ہے جو اڑ نہیں سکتا۔"
            },
            {
              "english": "Hold fast to dreams, for when dreams go, life is a barren field frozen with snow.",
              "urdu": "خوابوں کو مضبوطی سے تھامے رکھو، کیونکہ جب خواب رخصت ہو جاتے ہیں تو زندگی برف سے ڈھکا ہوا وہ بنجر کھیت ہے جس میں کچھ نہیں اگتا۔"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
