        "text": "The Iberian Peninsula, situated at the southwestern tip of Europe, was transformed by the arrival of Muslims in 711 AD under Tariq bin Ziyad. The historic city of Cordoba emerged as the radiant jewel of Al-Andalus and the capital of the Umayyad dynasty founded by Abd al-Rahman I in 756 AD. In Cordoba, he attempted to recreate the grandeur and cultural elegance of Damascus. While the rest of Europe languished in the Dark Ages, Muslim Spain shone as a glittering beacon of science, medicine, philosophy, literature, and architectural brilliance. Libraries, universities, hospitals, paved and illuminated streets made Cordoba the cultural capital of the medieval world.",
