        "headingPashto": "برخه 2: د قرطبې جومات او علامه اقبال",
        "text": "The most consummate and accomplished structure of the Masjid is its prayer hall. Begun in 784 AD by Abd al-Rahman I and expanded by subsequent rulers, the hall is erected with 857 majestic columns of jasper, onyx, marble, and granite from which sprout an amazing forest of two-tiered symmetrical arches. These double arches are composed of alternating keystones of red brick and white stone, creating a rhythmic chromatic effect and an impression of infinite spatial depth. The multiplicity of the columns in the prayer hall so amazed Allama Iqbal that he expressed his feelings in these memorable words:\n\n'Your foundations are lasting, your columns countless,\nLike the profusion of palms in the plains of Syria.'",
