        "headingPashto": "برخه 3: د قرطبې جومات او علامه اقبال",
        "text": "The focal point in the prayer hall is the famous horseshoe-arched Mehrab and the sacred Qibla wall. The arch and the Qibla wall of the Mehrab are decorated with the inscription of two lines of calligraphy in ornate Kufic style both on the top and on either side of the arch. The mosaic of the two lines of calligraphy has a deep blue background with shimmering gold lettering. The dome above the Mehrab is constructed with crisscrossing ribs that form an intricate radial star pattern, clad with dazzling Byzantine gold tesserae—individual glass cubes sandwiching pure gold leaf that produce an ethereal golden luster. Stylized vegetal motifs and geometric arabesques cover every surface, symbolizing the eternal and unsearchable infinity of Allah.",
