    "titleUrdu": "جنگ کے باوجود (نظم)",
    "titlePashto": "د جګړې سربېره (شعر)",
    "type": "poetry",
    "author": "Angela Morgan",
    "authorInfo": "Angela Morgan (1875–1957) was an American poet known for her vibrant, life-affirming verses celebrating nature's indomitable regenerative power amidst human devastation.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "1. Stanza 1: Blooming Flowers Amid Suffering and Wrath",
        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 1: جنگ کے باوجود (نظم)",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 1: د جګړې سربېره (شعر)",
        "text": "In spite of war, in spite of death,\nIn spite of all man's suffering,\nSomething within me laughs and sings\nAnd I must praise with all my breath.\nIn spite of war, in spite of hate,\nLilacs are blooming at my gate,\nIn spite of war, in spite of wrath,\n\"Courage!\" the morning-glory saith;\nAnd just to live is so divine\nWhen pansies lift their eyes to mine.",
        "paras": [
          "In spite of war, in spite of death,",
          "In spite of all man's suffering,",
          "Something within me laughs and sings",
          "And I must praise with all my breath.",
          "In spite of war, in spite of hate,",
          "Lilacs are blooming at my gate,",
          "In spite of war, in spite of wrath,",
          "\"Courage!\" the morning-glory saith;",
          "And just to live is so divine",
          "When pansies lift their eyes to mine."
        ],
        "urdu": "جنگ، نفرت اور تباہی کے باوجود دروازے پر کھلنے والے پھول اور صبح کی رونق شاعرہ کے دل میں جینے کی خوشی اور شکر گزاری پیدا کرتے ہیں۔",
        "pashto": "پښتو ترجمه او مفهوم: Stanza 1: Blooming Flowers Amid Suffering and Wrath"
      },
      {
        "heading": "2. Stanza 2: The Eternal Air and Nature's Unstoppable Splendor",
        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 2: جنگ کے باوجود (نظم)",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 2: د جګړې سربېره (شعر)",
        "text": "The clouds are vying with the sea,\nThe leaves are tripping in the tree;\nThat naught is real but what is fair,\nThat everywhere and everywhere\nA glory liveth through the air.\nThough guns may roar and cannon boom,\nRoses are born and gardens bloom;\nMy spirit still may catch its flame\nAt that same torch whence poppies came.",
        "paras": [
          "The clouds are vying with the sea,",
          "The leaves are tripping in the tree;",
          "That naught is real but what is fair,",
          "That everywhere and everywhere",
          "A glory liveth through the air.",
          "Though guns may roar and cannon boom,",
          "Roses are born and gardens bloom;",
          "My spirit still may catch its flame",
          "At that same torch whence poppies came."
        ],
        "urdu": "توپوں کی گھن گرج کے باوجود باغوں میں گلاب کھلتے ہیں اور فطرت کی خوبصورتی ثابت کرتی ہے کہ اصل سچائی حسن اور زندگی ہی ہے۔",
        "pashto": "پښتو ترجمه او مفهوم: Stanza 2: The Eternal Air and Nature's Unstoppable Splendor"
      },
      {
        "heading": "3. Stanza 3: Awakening from the Nightmare to Divine Ecstasy",
        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 3: جنگ کے باوجود (نظم)",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 3: د جګړې سربېره (شعر)",
        "text": "Where morning's altar whitely burns\nLilies may lift their silver urns\nIn spite of war, in spite of shame.\nAnd in my ear, a whispering breath:\n\"Wake from the nightmare! Look and see\nThat life is naught but ecstasy\nIn spite of war, in spite of death!\"",
        "paras": [
          "Where morning's altar whitely burns",
          "Lilies may lift their silver urns",
          "In spite of war, in spite of shame.",
          "And in my ear, a whispering breath:",
          "\"Wake from the nightmare! Look and see",
          "That life is naught but ecstasy",
          "In spite of war, in spite of death!\""
        ],
        "urdu": "شاعرہ انسان کو جنگ کے خوفناک خواب سے جاگنے کا پیغام دیتی ہے کیونکہ زندگی کی اصل حقیقت خوشی اور لازوال روحانی مسرت ہے۔",
        "pashto": "پښتو ترجمه او مفهوم: Stanza 3: Awakening from the Nightmare to Divine Ecstasy"
      },
      {
        "heading": "4. About the Poet (Angela Morgan)",
        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 4: جنگ کے باوجود (نظم)",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 4: د جګړې سربېره (شعر)",
        "text": "Angela Morgan was born in 1875 in Washington, D.C. Her given name at birth was Nina Lillian, which she later changed to Angela. Her career as a writer started as a journalist for the Chicago and New York newspapers before World War I. Her most productive years were from 1914–1940. Morgan's pieces were published in major magazines. She also wrote fourteen books of poetry and stories. She passed away on January 24, 1957, in New York.",
        "paras": [
          "Angela Morgan was born in 1875 in Washington, D.C. Her given name at birth was Nina Lillian, which she later changed to Angela. Her career as a writer started as a journalist for the Chicago and New York newspapers before World War I. Her most productive years were from 1914–1940. Morgan's pieces were published in major magazines. She also wrote fourteen books of poetry and stories. She passed away on January 24, 1957, in New York."
        ],
        "urdu": "امریکی شاعرہ اور صحافی اینجلا مورگن کا تعارف جن کی شاعری جنگ کے دوران امن، امید اور زندگی کے جذبے کا مظہر ہے۔",
        "pashto": "پښتو ترجمه او مفهوم: About the Poet (Angela Morgan)"
      }
    ],
    "pashtoTranslation": "دا نظم د جګړې او ورانۍ سره سره د طبیعت د ژوندۍ ښکلا او د هیلو د بریا پیغام وړاندې کوي.",
    "englishTranslation": "Angela Morgan's poem 'In Spite of War' is a passionate declaration of hope and the triumph of nature over human violence. Even when artillery roars and armies clash, lilac blossoms bloom, morning sunshine radiates golden warmth, and birds sing melodies of renewal, proving life is resilient and divine love indestructible.",
