      "writingTasks": [
        {
          "summary": "In the moving Japanese folktale 'The Aged Mother', adapted by Matsuo Basho, the cruel governor of Shinano province decrees that all elderly citizens must be put to death due to his cowardly fear of infirmity. A loving young farmer tearfully carries his widowed mother up the rugged slopes of Mount Obatsuyama to abandon her to a gentle death. Along the arduous climb, the mother selflessly snaps branches and drops twigs along the path so her son will not lose his way returning home in the dark. Deeply moved by this supreme demonstration of maternal love, the son refuses to leave her. He carries her back down, concealing her in a secret closet under his kitchen floor. When the governor later challenges the province to produce an impossible 'rope of ashes', the mother's wisdom guides the son to burn twisted straw on flat stones on a windless night. Presenting the flawless rope of ashes, the youth courageously confesses his secret. Amazed by her genius, the governor repents, acknowledging that 'with the crown of snow comes wisdom', permanently repealing the cruel decree and restoring honor to all elderly citizens.",
          "essay": {
            "title": "Respect for Parents and Senior Citizens in Modern Society",
            "text": "The Japanese folktale 'The Aged Mother' delivers a timeless moral message on the sanctity of parents and the invaluable role of senior citizens. In contemporary consumerist societies, there is an alarming tendency among modern youth to regard aging parents as financial or social liabilities, overlooking the immense sacrifices made in raising them. Senior citizens possess a lifetime of accumulated wisdom, moral patience, and practical insight that no textbook or algorithm can replicate. True civilizational maturity is demonstrated not by the speed of economic growth, but by the dignity and gratitude with which a society treats its elderly. Youth must realize that honoring parents is both a divine religious commandment and a fundamental ethical obligation. When we protect, consult, and revere our elders, we enrich our homes with spiritual blessing and preserve the cultural wisdom essential for human flourishing."
          },
          "translationUrdu": [
            {
              "english": "The poor farmer loved his mother with tender reverence, and the cruel decree filled his heart with profound grief.",
              "urdu": "غریب کسان اپنی بوڑھی ماں سے انتہائی عقیدت اور محبت کرتا تھا، اور اس ظالمانہ حکم نے اس کے دل کو شدید غم سے بھر دیا۔"
            },
            {
              "english": "Oh, honorable mother, your kindness breaks my heart! I will not leave you. Together we will follow the path of twigs, and together we will die!",
              "urdu": "اے محترم ماں! آپ کی اس شفقت نے میرا دل چیر دیا ہے! میں آپ کو کبھی نہیں چھوڑوں گا۔ ہم ساتھ مل کر ٹہنیوں کے راستے پر چلیں گے اور ساتھ ہی جئیں اور مریں گے!"
            },
            {
              "english": "With the crown of snow, there cometh wisdom!",
              "urdu": "سفید بالوں (بڑھاپے کے تاج) کے ساتھ ہی دانائی اور حکمت آتی ہے!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
