          "topic": "Prepositions of Time and Place (Exercise B)",
          "rule": "Prepositions of time and place indicate when or where an event occurs: 'at' (precise clock times, specific points), 'in' (months, years, enclosed spaces), 'on' (days, dates, surfaces), 'since' (from a specific point in the past until now).",
