        "headingPashto": "برخه 2: په پاکستان کې د اوبو د کمښت بحران",
        "text": "Beneath the soil, groundwater serves as the second most vital reservoir for domestic, industrial, and agricultural use. Over 1.2 million private and public tube-wells pump groundwater relentlessly across the Punjab, Sindh, and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa plains. However, unregulated over-pumping has triggered catastrophic groundwater depletion. Water tables that once lay 20 to 30 feet below ground level have plummeted to depths of several hundred feet in major cities like Quetta, Lahore, and Islamabad.\n\nIf current extraction rates continue, water demand will almost double by the year 2025, subjecting underground aquifers to irreversible saline contamination and exhaustion. Climate change, retreating glaciers in the northern highlands, and erratic rainfall patterns further compound this existential vulnerability.",
