        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 4: پاکستان میں پانی کی قلت کا بحران",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 4: په پاکستان کې د اوبو د کمښت بحران",
        "text": "The problems faced by the water sector are acute, urgent, and complex. Therefore, constructing major and medium storage reservoirs, lining irrigation canals to eliminate seepage, and adopting effective water management policies are the paramount needs of the hour.\n\nIn agriculture, which consumes over 90% of our water, Pakistan must urgently transition from wasteful flood irrigation to conservation agriculture and micro-irrigation technologies:\n1. Sprinkler Irrigation: A method of applying water similar to natural rainfall, distributed through pressurized pipes and sprayed uniformly over crops, cutting water waste by 40%.\n2. Drip Irrigation: A high-efficiency technique where water flows through filters and dripper pipes directly to the plant root zones, saving up to 70% of water while boosting crop yields.\n3. Laser Land Leveling and Rainwater Harvesting: Ensuring uniform water distribution in fields and capturing rooftop stormwater in cities.\n\nIt is widely acknowledged that the wars of the twenty-first century will be fought over water resources. We must save water now to secure our economic survival, guarantee food security, and prevent future geopolitical conflict.",
