        "headingUrdu": "حصہ 1: ماڈل لکھ پتی",
        "headingPashto": "برخه 1: نمونه میلیونر (ماډل ملینیر)",
        "text": "Hughie Erskine was a wonderfully handsome, soft-hearted, and well-mannered young gentleman with brown curly hair, clear grey eyes, and a graceful profile. He was universally popular in London society because of his agreeable demeanor, generous heart, and unaffected simplicity. Intellectually, however, he was not of much importance: he had never said a brilliant or even an unkind thing in his life. Moreover, he was notoriously ineffectual in business. He had once been a tea merchant, but a sudden slump in the tea trade wiped out his capital. He then tried selling dry sherry, but that did not answer. Next, he attempted stock exchange speculation, but that ended in a fiasco. Ultimately, he became a charming young man with no profession, living upon an allowance of two hundred pounds a year made to him by an old aunt.",
