          "rule": "1. Dash (—): Indicates an abrupt break in thought, dramatic emphasis, or parenthesis.\n2. Ellipsis (...): Marks an omission of words from a quotation or a trailing off in speech.\n3. Brackets ([ ]): Enclose editorial additions, clarifications, or missing words within a quotation.",
