    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:2,printedPage:null,title:'Urdu quotations',sourceLanguage:'ur',text:'مومن تو آپس میں بھائی بھائی ہیں۔ پس اپنے دو بھائیوں میں صلح کرا دیا کرو اور اللہ سے ڈرتے رہو تاکہ تم پر رحم کیا جائے۔ (سورۃ الحجرات: 10)\nرشوت اور بدعنوانی قومی معیشت کو کھوکھلا کر دیتی ہے۔ قومی معیشت کو کھوکھلا ہونے سے بچانے میں اپنا کردار ادا کریں۔'},
    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:3,printedPage:'i',title:'Internal title page',text:'Printed title: A textbook of English, Grade X. Handwritten reader marks and notes cover parts of this scan; they are annotations, not textbook content.'},
    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:4,printedPage:'ii',title:'Copyright, approval and contributors',text:'All rights reserved with Leading Books Publishers, Peshawar. Developed according to the National Curriculum 2006 and approved by Directorate of Curriculum & Teacher Education (DCTE), Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Abbottabad. NOC No. 5720-23/F03/Vol-I/Eng-X(LBP), dated 28-11-2018. Developed by Leading Books Publishers, Peshawar. Authors: Ms. Aamna Aamad (M.A. English Literature), freelance consultant; Ali Akbar Khan, Assistant Professor (English), Government College Lakaro, District Mohmand. Review supervision: Gohar Ali Khan, Director Curriculum & Teacher Education, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Abbottabad. Focal person: Zulfiqar Khan, Additional Director (Curriculum & Textbook Review), Directorate of Curriculum & Teachers Education, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Abbottabad. Re-reviewers: Amin Dad; Qazi Saeed Ahmed; Baber Ayaz; Waheedullah; Inamullah Khattak. Editor: Najma Khalique, Subject Specialist (English), Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board, Peshawar. Printing supervision: Abidullah Kakakhel, Chairman; Abdul Wali Khan, Member (E&P), Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board, Peshawar. Printed for Academic Year 2026–2027. Website: www.kptbb.gov.pk; email: membertbb@yahoo.com; telephone: 091-9217714-15. Marked “Not For Sale”.'},
    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:5,printedPage:'iii',title:'Introduction',text:'This revised edition of English Textbook for Grade X contains material from the original book as well as new entries agreed upon by English subject experts at the Textbook Board, DCTE and private sector. The overall revision of the current edition was undertaken to align the textbook, amongst others, with the Standards for textbooks included in the Minimum National Standards for Quality Education in Pakistan. Therefore, the current revised edition has been revised with a view to make it a more representative textbook of the National Curriculum 2006; in content and organisation, presentation, layout, assessment, cultural values and elimination of all forms of biases. This revised version of the textbook comprises new essays, stories, poems, lessons, illustrations, fresh layout and design. The exercises have been carefully designed under new headings and now include speaking and listening components designed to develop oral-aural language skills. The exercises provide ample opportunities for practice and contain drill work as well as imaginative/creative tasks. The exercises are based on these headings: Context—wide variety of reading material, including factual accounts, stories based on nature, environment, fantasy, adventures, fables and poetry. Comprehension—relating directly to the context, to develop the child’s ability to read and comprehend. Grammar—including formal areas of language study, syntax, structure, punctuation and its usage. The language and grammatical structures are elementary; there is ample revision and repetition. Composition/writing—developing functional and creative writing skills. Listening and speaking—involving listening skills, proper pronunciation, structure, functional vocabulary, expression and debating skills. Signed “Editor”.'},
    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:6,printedPage:'iv',title:'Table of Contents, units 1–8',text:'The table columns are number, unit, theme and vocabulary. Entries: 1, Simplicity and Humility of Hazrat Muhammad—Simplicity—word definition, guide words, entry words, pronunciation through pronunciation key. 2, The Champions (Adapted from Amigo Brothers by Piri Thomas)—Learning to live together in extended society, interculturally and at national level—word definition, part of speech. 3, Dreams (By Langston Hughes)—Ambition—word definition with evidence from text. 4, Population Growth and its Impact on Environment—impact of population growth on environment, health and nutrition—word definition, part of speech. 5, The Great Masjid of Cordoba and Iqbal—places of historical/cultural importance and of interest around the world—pronunciation, synonyms. 6, In Spite Of War (By Angela Morgan)—optimism/hope—words that evoke negative and positive connotations. 7, The Aged Mother—respecting self and others—word meaning, guide and entry words, part of speech. 8, Women’s Role in the Pakistan Movement—understanding/practicing gender equality—context clues and root meaning.'},
    {pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:7,printedPage:'v',title:'Table of Contents, skills by unit',text:'The table columns are Listening & Speaking, Comprehension, Grammar, Writing and page. Unit 1, page 1: group presentation on simplicity and humility of the beloved Rasool, Hazrat Muhammad; questions and answers, MCQs; nouns (countable/uncountable, collective, material/abstract), number nouns and nouns changing meaning in plural (e.g. arm/arms); summary of lesson and translation. Unit 2, page 10: present and explain a point of view/feeling about “The Champions”; articles, pronouns, relative/indefinite pronouns, antecedent agreement; paragraph and dialogue writing. Unit 3, page 22: share future dreams/aspirations; transitive/intransitive verbs, present/past participles, clauses; persuasive essay “A dream doesn’t become reality through magic; it takes sweat, determination and hard work.” Unit 4, page 31: share information/ideas about population growth; present perfect continuous and past perfect continuous; paragraph “We Cannot Afford Deforestation Because It Will Add Air Pollution.” Unit 5, page 40: discuss downfall of Muslim rule in Spain; adjective types/degrees and adjective formation; spatial-order paragraph, expository essay with mind map. Unit 6, page 55: presentation on “O peace! How many wars were waged in thy name”; adjective phrase/clause; paraphrase and poem summary. Unit 7, page 63: role-play greetings, compliments, invitations, introductions and farewells; modal verbs, regular/irregular verbs; paragraph/essay writing, lesson summary and translation. Unit 8, page 74: presentation on diverse roles Pakistani women play in households; adverb degree/position/kinds, adverbial phrases, comparison of adverbs/phrases/clauses; organization patterns for essay paragraphs.'}
