eng10Unit6.sourcePages.push({pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:69,printedPage:'62',title:'Unit 6 adjective-phrase and adjective-clause exercises',text:'A asks learners to underline adjective phrases in five sentences about an elephant, a gold crown, a girl with blue eyes, wild beasts in small cages and a man with a long beard. B replaces bold adjectives with phrases in six sentences (golden, white, stone, earthen, diamond, brave). C identifies adjective clauses and the nouns modified in five sentences. D combines five pairs of simple sentences into complex sentences containing adjective clauses.'});
