{pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:141,printedPage:'134',title:'Hazrat Umar writing, speaking and active/passive voice',text:'Writing asks for a lesson summary, a persuasive essay on Umar serving his countrymen as a servant, and Urdu translation of the hungry-children incident. Speaking asks for a fact-supported presentation comparing Umar’s administration with Pakistan today. Grammar defines active/passive voice and gives five paired transformations: Saleem changed the flat tyre; I ran the obstacle course; Mom read the novel; I will clean the house; Tahir painted the house.'},
{pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:142,printedPage:'135',title:'Active and passive voice exercises',text:'Exercise A asks learners to label eight sentences active or passive. Exercise B rewrites eight passive sentences in active voice, including sentences about grammar taught by Mrs Sikandar, a teacher’s praise, injured people taken to hospital, a town destroyed by earthquake, a teacher pleased, a fire-damaged building, an English lesson, and a ticket given by the manager.'}
