{pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:153,printedPage:'146',title:'Polite refusals and reported statements',text:'Gives polite refusals to requests, offers and social invitations with sample phrases. Grammar A asks learners to change five assertive sentences into indirect speech: boys’ statement about rain; a woman leaving and returning; a girl’s father buying toys; a husband not going to office because he is unwell; and a father saying someone has caught a cold again.'},
{pdf:'10th english.pdf',pdfPage:154,printedPage:'147',title:'Reported questions, exclamations and commands',text:'Exercise B changes five interrogative sentences to indirect speech; C changes five exclamatory sentences; D changes five imperative sentences. Prompts include medicine use, lending a book, offering help, coming home on time, warning beforehand, a beautiful child, a pleasant surprise, feeling unlucky, praise, losing a game, leaving a room, bringing water, not wasting time, working hard and not smoking.'}
