 {q:'He should come to the meetings on time. Options: (a) to convey the idea of an obligation; (b) to make a suggestion or advice; (c) for prohibition; (d) to form polite questions.'},
 {q:'Can you help me with this exercise? Options: (a) to show inability or impossibility; (b) to express or inquire about willingness; (c) to show possibility; (d) to express permission.'},
 {q:'You needn’t take your umbrella. It isn’t raining. Options: (a) expressing prohibition; (b) expressing obligation; (c) expressing lack of necessity; (d) expressing ability.'},
 {q:'Could you say it again more slowly? Options: (a) to make a request; (b) to give a suggestion; (c) to show ability in the past; (d) to identify a possibility.'},
 {q:'The weather will be hot enough to go to the beach this weekend. Options: (a) to express intention; (b) to make a prediction; (c) for habitual behavior; (d) to show willingness or interest.'},
 {q:'The dog would bark every time the doorbell rang. Options: (a) to request permission; (b) for preferences; (c) for requests; (d) to show habitual activity.'},
 {q:'Shall I help you with your luggage? Options: (a) for suggestions; (b) for offering someone help; (c) for asking what to do; (d) to indicate a promise.'}
